  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Using family of planes, equation to plane passing through the line of intersection of the given planes, is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>If a&nbsp;plane is perpendicular to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi></math>&nbsp;plane, then it doesn&#39;t contain the term of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Thus, the plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>The length of perpendicular from a point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;to the plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><msqrt><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, required perpendicular distance of point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from plane is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn></mrow><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mfenced></math>&nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>&nbsp;units.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
